  "description": "The services ICP (Oct 22, 2026): operators (founders up to Series C and SMB owners) with a US entity and USD books who want the bookkeeping done for them. The default pipeline.",
  "provisional": [
    "Decided 2026-11-03: Series C is in; the $500K monthly-expense ceiling is the proxy NetSuite with a finance team (W10), Series D or later (S6) or 100+ people (S7); 50-99 people (S8) only scores down",
    "Books behind (S3), looking for help (S4) and DIY (S5) are rarely public; Unknown stays Unknown",
    "Weights and the Strong-fit cut-off (decided 2026-11-13, no input from Puzzle): kept as set; for cold outreach the score only orders the approved leads (Outreach priority A/B/C). They can be calibrated later with labelled companies (python -m enrich calibrate)",
    "Decided 2026-11-07 (Alexey): young companies lose no points for being young; AI companies lose no points (Puzzle's MCP lets them do the books with their own agent), so does-its-own-books (S5) is info and routes to Platform + MCP; real estate and legal pass with 'ask how the books are handled'",
    "website_optional (2026-11-09, turned off 2026-11-13): no working website (a 404, a coming-soon or parked page, a dead domain) is a hard No on M2: cold outreach skips leads without a website. A pre-launch company with a real site and a waitlist still passes (Yes (pre-launch)), and so does a site that was blocked or timed out (retry).",
    "Cold outreach (2026-11-12): the model should only reject what Puzzle can't serve. Pre-launch companies (a waitlist or coming-soon page, no sales yet) are not failed on M2/M4: they pass as 'Yes (pre-launch)', lose 2 points (W5) and are contacted last; 11 of 82 real leads were pre-launch and several bought. Holding stock (E6), marketplace (S2), running several US companies (F17), a new subsidiary (B8) and non-profit (E5) are weak signals (-2, check on the call) instead of hard stops: final (decided 2026-11-13 on the 82 real leads; Verse, SEYA, Wealthie, BoxHero, Phoenix Bikes and the church were real leads, several won). Hard stops left: outside the US, accounting firm, sole proprietorship, multi-currency, manufacturing, too big."
